  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The amount $C$ of a carbon isotope in a dead tree trunk is given by $C=C_0e^{-kt}$, where $t$ is measured in years from the death of the tree, and $k$ is a positive constant.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain the significance of $C_0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$C_0$ is the amount of the carbon isotope in the tree at the time of its death.",
          "worked": "At the time of death, $t=0$, so $C=C_0e^0=C_0$. Thus $C_0$ is the initial amount of the carbon isotope.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find $k$, correct to four significant figures, if the half-life of the isotope is 6000 years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=1.155\\times10^{-4}\\ \\text{year}^{-1}$.",
          "worked": "At half-life, $C=\\dfrac{C_0}{2}$ when $t=6000$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{C_0}{2}&=C_0e^{-6000k}\\\\\\frac12&=e^{-6000k}\\\\-6000k&=\\ln\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\\\-6000k&=-\\ln2\\\\k&=\\frac{\\ln2}{6000}\\\\k&\\approx1.155\\times10^{-4}\\ \\text{year}^{-1}\\quad\\text{(4 significant figures)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "A dead tree trunk has 12% of the amount of the isotope compared to what a typical living tree would have. How many years ago did the tree die, correct to the nearest 1000 years?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "18 000 years ago.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}0.12C_0&=C_0e^{-kt}\\\\0.12&=e^{-kt}\\\\-kt&=\\ln(0.12)\\\\t&=-\\frac{\\ln(0.12)}{k}\\\\t&=-\\frac{\\ln(0.12)}{\\ln2/6000}\\\\t&\\approx18353.36\\ \\text{years}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe tree died 18 000 years ago, to the nearest 1000 years.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      }
    ]
  },
